      "side": 1,
      "message": "I thought I saw so many issues here, until it finally sunk in that these AddFarVariantionDependencies calls only exist to generate errors. To be fair the comments do point that out, but still.\n\n- I suggest adding a wrapper in android/mutator.go so that these calls can read\n\n  ctx.ReportMissingDependencyError(variations, tag, foo)\n\ninstead, and then its implementation calls AddFarVariationDependencies.\n\n- Besides being confusing, can\u0027t it also lead to tricky bugs? I.e. if we get a logic bug so that these calls are done in the wrong code paths and actually are successful. It would be good to check afterwards that they did indeed report an error, but I don\u0027t know offhand how easy that is to do.",
      "revId": "2120ee6261c5afa1fd763796c527bab5ff785334",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1415f55e_0842a639",
        "filename": "java/platform_bootclasspath.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
